# Kconfig fragment: nftables address families + conntrack match (2026-10-15).
#
# Listed in amdkdehard's PROF_LIVE_KFRAGS (2026-10-16; first nvidiahard-only
# on 10-15), so every hard profile derived from it carries it — not in the
# shared live.fragment, so the desktop images stay without the attack surface
# described below. For h5i's 'supervised' sandbox tier. h5i enforces a box's
# egress allowlist with an nft ruleset inside the box's own network namespace:
#   table inet h5i_egress { chain output { ... policy drop;
#     ct state established,related accept; ip daddr <api ip> tcp dport 443 accept } }
# live.fragment carries NF_TABLES=m but NO family, so 'nft' gets EOPNOTSUPP on
# 'table inet' and every supervised run with a non-empty egress list fails
# ("supervised spawn failed: Invalid argument").
#
# Pure additions: nothing else is switched off. INET is bool, depends on IPV6,
# and SELECTS IPV4 + IPV6 (both bool, built into nf_tables.ko since
# NF_TABLES=m); they are named anyway so the post-merge check can see them.
# NFT_CT is the 'ct' expression, depends on NF_CONNTRACK (=m in live.fragment).
#
# What it costs (why it is NOT in the shared live.fragment; verified working
# on nvhard 2026-10-16 — supervised box reaches only its allowlist):
#   * Attack surface. Any unprivileged user can create a user + network
#     namespace and load nft rules into it. Without a family that path stops
#     at table creation; with one, the nf_tables set/verdict code becomes
#     reachable from a normal user — historically a busy source of local
#     privilege-escalation bugs (CVE-2024-1086 and others). Keep the kernel on
#     current stable updates while this is on.
#   * Backend auto-detection. Programs that prefer nftables when it works start
#     using it. Checked 2026-10-15: docker 29 (backend iptables, explicit),
#     netavark 1.17 (iptables default), tailscale ('ipt-default'), the hardened
#     iptables ruleset — none move. netavark >= 2.0 DEFAULTS TO nftables; with
#     the hardened FORWARD DROP in iptables, rootful podman forwarding would
#     then be dropped silently. Pin firewall_driver = "iptables" in
#     /etc/containers/containers.conf before netavark 2.x arrives.
# Drop this fragment from the profile to undo; nothing else depends on it.
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_INET=y
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_CT=m
